--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 146b4dedcb9af3b4ab5fe5794271c3d8, type: 3}
  m_Name: Ticket_Coc1_Gpu_Missing
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::TicketData
  ticketId: ticket_coc1_gpu_missing
  targetModule: 0
  sceneName: COC1-Copy
  title: No display after the unit was moved
  description: The PC was carried to another room. It powers on normally - fans and
    lights are fine - but the monitor stays black. The same monitor worked before
    the move.
  icon: {fileID: 0}
  briefingDialog: {fileID: 0}
  requiredTaskId: ticket_coc1_gpu_missing
  requiresDiagnosis: 1
  symptomText: System powers on. Fans and drive activity normal. No POST beep. No
    signal on the monitor connected to the graphics card port.
  diagnosisOptions:
  - label: Graphics card not properly seated
    isCorrect: 1
    feedback: Correct. Transporting a unit is a classic cause of an expansion card
      working loose. Reseat it fully and check the retention clip.
  - label: Faulty monitor or video cable
    isCorrect: 0
    feedback: Worth ruling out and cheap to test - but the customer says the same
      monitor worked before the move, which points inside the case.
  - label: Failed power supply
    isCorrect: 0
    feedback: The fans and lights are running, so the PSU is delivering power.
  - label: Corrupted operating system
    isCorrect: 0
    feedback: An OS fault still shows POST and a boot screen first. A completely
      black display means the problem is earlier than the OS.
